          "type": "concept",
          "title": "DSHEA 1994: The Law That Built the Aisle",
          "content": "The modern supplement market was shaped by one law: the **Dietary Supplement Health and Education Act of 1994 (DSHEA)**. It classified vitamins, minerals, herbs, amino acids and similar products as a special category of **food**, not drugs.\n\nWhat that means in practice:\n• **No pre-market approval** -- a company does not need FDA permission to sell a supplement\n• **No proof it works** -- efficacy trials are not required\n• **The manufacturer is responsible for safety** -- but does not have to show the FDA its data first\n• **The burden flips** -- to pull a product, the FDA generally has to show it is unsafe after it is already on shelves\n• **New ingredients** introduced after 1994 need a safety notification, but compliance has been spotty\n\nDSHEA passed with enormous public support -- people wanted access. The tradeoff is that **you**, the shopper, are doing much of the vetting a regulator would do for a drug.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">DSHEA 1994 IN FOUR RULES</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Supplements are regulated like food</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"440\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">NO PRE-APPROVAL</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Sell first, questions later</text><rect x=\"580\" y=\"170\" width=\"440\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">NO EFFICACY PROOF</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Trials are optional</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"400\" width=\"440\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"470\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">MAKER OWNS SAFETY</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Data not filed up front</text><rect x=\"580\" y=\"400\" width=\"440\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"470\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">FDA MUST PROVE HARM</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Mostly after the fact</text></svg>",
            "caption": "The four rules DSHEA set in 1994 still govern the aisle today"
          }
