          "explanation": "Creatine breaks down to creatinine, the marker labs use to estimate kidney function, so supplement users (and very muscular people) can show a higher creatinine and a lower estimated GFR without any kidney damage. A test like cystatin C, which is not affected by creatine or muscle mass, can clarify. The tempting wrong answer assumes damage -- but in healthy people, long-term studies have not shown kidney harm at normal doses.",
