          "explanation": "Since 1998 the FDA has allowed a health claim that soluble fiber from psyllium, as part of a diet low in saturated fat, may reduce heart disease risk. Meta-analyses show roughly 10 g/day lowers LDL by about 13 mg/dL. Collagen's vessel-wall pitch is the tempting distractor -- it sounds biological, but there is no authorized claim or solid trial evidence behind it. Protein powders have no heart health claim at all.",
