          "explanation": "Six months of poor sleep most nights fits chronic insomnia, and the American College of Physicians recommends CBT-I as first-line treatment -- it works as well as pills short term and keeps working afterward. Melatonin only shaves minutes off sleep onset for insomnia, and higher doses mostly add grogginess, so doubling it is the tempting but wrong move. Stacking valerian (weak evidence) and ashwagandha (liver caveats) adds risk. CFU is a probiotic measure, not a melatonin one.",
